---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE, buyHref } from "../config";
import { getPosts, formatDate, readingMinutes } from "../lib/blog";

const site = Astro.site!.href.replace(/\/$/, "");
const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: site + "/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: 'Privacy', item: site + '/privacy/' },
    ],
  },
];
---
<Base
  title='Privacy: what BoltGrab stores and sends'
  description='What BoltGrab keeps on your PC, the few optional features that contact other services, and how this website counts visits. No ads and no tracking in the app.'
  current=''
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="page-head">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p>The BoltGrab app has no ads and no tracking. This page lists what it keeps, every optional feature that contacts another service, and how this website counts visits.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="fine">Draft for review before launch: please have it checked against your final product, payment provider and local law.</p>

      <h2>What stays on your PC</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your download list, queues, categories and settings are stored in a file on your PC.</li>
        <li>Passwords for downloads that need a login are kept in the Windows Credential Manager, not in that file.</li>
        <li>The browser extension sends links, file names and the cookies needed for a download only to BoltGrab on your own PC (the address 127.0.0.1). Cookies are not stored on disk by the extension.</li>
        <li>Your license is checked on your PC against a digital signature. It does not need the internet.</li>
        <li>BoltGrab does not send usage statistics or crash reports.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>When BoltGrab contacts other services</h2>
      <p>Only for the things you ask it to do, or the optional features below.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>The downloads themselves.</b> BoltGrab connects to the websites you download from, just like a browser would.</li>
        <li><b>VirusTotal check (off by default).</b> If you add your own API key, BoltGrab sends the SHA-256 fingerprint of a finished file to VirusTotal. The file is never uploaded.</li>
        <li><b>Video components.</b> The first time a video needs them, BoltGrab downloads two small helper components from their publishers' official download sites (GitHub and gyan.dev) and verifies each against the publisher's checksum. The video component is refreshed about weekly unless you switch that off.</li>
        <li><b>Speed test.</b> Only when you open it: it measures against Cloudflare's speed servers.</li>
        <li><b>Trusted Sites.</b> The page shows each listed site's own icon, which your PC loads from that site when you open the page.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <h3>Visit statistics (Google Analytics)</h3>
      <p>The public pages of this website (home, features, pricing, blog and this page) use Google Analytics 4 to count visits: which pages are read, roughly where visitors come from (country level), and what device and browser they use. Google sets cookies named <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code> for this, and the page loads Google's script from googletagmanager.com. We have switched off Google's advertising features, so the data is not used for ad personalization. The statistics are used only to improve the website.</p>
      <p>Analytics is not loaded on the sign-in, sign-up, account, purchase, thank-you or admin pages. It is also not loaded if your browser sends a Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signal. You can also block it with a browser tracking-protection setting or an ad blocker. The BoltGrab app itself does not use Google Analytics.</p>

      <h3>Accounts and sign-in</h3>
      <p>Only if you create an account or sign in: we set a session cookie so you stay signed in, the sign-in and sign-up pages load Google's sign-in button, and the phone-number field shows country flag images from flagcdn.com. Our hosting provider may keep standard server logs for security and reliability.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>

</Base>
